  /Alt (This conceptual diagram illustrates a land cover change from 2012 to 2018, as observed in general imagery ('IMAGE') and specifically within the Riparian Zones (RZ) product. The diagram consists of four panels arranged chronologically (2012, 2018) for two product types (IMAGE, RZ). 1. **IMAGE 2012:** Displays a large light green area labelled '4.2.x' with a nested, unlabelled light green rectangular polygon, implying a uniform land cover of class '4.2.x'. 2. **IMAGE 2018:** The central nested polygon has changed to blue and is labelled '8.2.3', while the surrounding area remains light green '4.2.x'. This represents a land cover change from class '4.2.x' to '8.2.3' within the central polygon. Based on the surrounding text, '8.2.3' likely represents a water surface. 3. **RZ 2012:** The Riparian Zones (RZ) product for 2012 reflects the base land cover, showing the central nested polygon as light green and labelled '4.2.x', consistent with the general imagery. 4. **RZ 2018:** The Riparian Zones (RZ) product for 2018 shows the central nested polygon as blue and labelled '8.2.3', indicating that the change detected in the general imagery is also captured and represented in the RZ product. The diagram demonstrates how a land cover change of a polygon is consistently mapped in the Riparian Zones product between 2012 and 2018.)
  /A [<<
    /O /Layout
    /Placement /Block
